Sval: Settings name the home page beside the address bar

The home page's field answers from the address bar's engine
(SvalHomeSearchParent), so the address bar's suggestion settings govern it too.
Their labels say so. Fluent strings have no override short of a patch.

diff --git a/browser/locales/en-US/browser/preferences/preferences.ftl b/browser/locales/en-US/browser/preferences/preferences.ftl
index 1516c920c4..2bf96d0790 100644
--- a/browser/locales/en-US/browser/preferences/preferences.ftl
+++ b/browser/locales/en-US/browser/preferences/preferences.ftl
@@ -1096,7 +1096,7 @@ search-show-suggestions-url-bar-option =
 # "before" refers to location (appearing most proximate to), not time
 # (appearing before).
 search-show-suggestions-above-history-option-2 =
-    .label = Show search suggestions before browsing history in address bar results
+    .label = Show search suggestions before browsing history in address bar and home page results
 
 search-show-suggestions-private-windows-2 =
     .label = Search suggestions in private windows
@@ -1105,8 +1105,8 @@ search-suggestions-cant-show-2 =
     .message = Search suggestions will not be shown in location bar results because you have configured { -brand-short-name } to never remember history.
 
 addressbar-header-1 =
-    .label = Address Bar
-    .description = Choose which suggestions display in your address bar
+    .label = Address Bar and Home Page
+    .description = Choose which suggestions display in your address bar and on your home page
 
 # When Firefox Suggest is enabled, this replaces `addressbar-header-1`.
 addressbar-header-firefox-suggest-2 =
